  tempDescriptions:
  - A piano is a keyboard instrument that produces sound when its keys are pressed,
  - "activating an action mechanism where hammers strike strings. Modern pianos have
    a row of 88 black and white keys\u2014"
  - "with the exception of the Bosend\xF6rfer and Stuart & Sons pianos"
  - 'There are two main types of piano: the grand piano and the upright piano.'
